IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch5`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 5, paragraphs 3C to 9: pension increase or lump sum where the deceased spouse or civil partner (S) had deferred
-- entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension, and the widow, widower or surviving civil partner (W) is entitled.
-- The pensioner's own paragraphs (A1 to 3B) are in ssc9-sch5.l4, which this module imports.
-- The converter dropped the paragraph numbers; the labels follow in-text citations (3C, 4, 5, 5A, 6, 6A, 7, 7A, 7B, 7C, 8)
-- and two are inferred (the unnumbered paragraph that modifies 5A to 6A, and the last paragraph "Uprating", read as 9): NOTES.md.
-- Dates are `Date day month year`. Money is a NUMBER in pounds, weekly unless the name says otherwise.

§ `Schedule 5 -- paragraphs 3C to 9: where the deceased spouse or civil partner had deferred entitlement`

§§ `Paragraph 3C -- choice between increase of pension and lump sum`

-- 3C(2): what W elects between.
DECLARE `sch 5 Widowed election` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 para 3C(2)(a) an election that paragraph 4 (the increase of pension) applies`
    `sch 5 para 3C(2)(b) an election that paragraph 7A (the lump sum) applies`

DECLARE `sch 5 W Party` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 W the widow, widower or surviving civil partner`

DECLARE `sch 5 W Act` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 W makes an election` HAS `the choice` IS A `sch 5 Widowed election`

-- 8(4) (read with 3C(1)(c)): a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W's
-- contributions does not satisfy the conditions in 3C(1)(c) and 4(1)(a). A flat negative; any other pension is not spoken to.
-- src:5288 | (4) The conditions in paragraph 3C(1)(c) and 4(1)(a) are not satisfied by a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W’s contributions.
@ref sch 5 para 8(4) (src:5288)
GIVEN `S’s pension is a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W’s contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 8(4) the conditions in paragraphs 3C(1)(c) and 4(1)(a) are satisfied by S’s pension` MEANS
    IF `S’s pension is a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W’s contributions`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are not satisfied by a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W’s contributions"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph speaks only of a Category B pension earned by W's contributions

-- 3C(1): applies where (a) W is entitled to a Category A or B pension, (b) W was married to or the civil partner of S when S died,
-- (c) S's entitlement was deferred when S died, and (d) S's entitlement had been deferred throughout the 12 months ending with the
-- day before S's death. Subject to paragraph 8 (8(4) above). The 12 months are those of ssc9-sch5 (paragraph A1(1) at least 12 months)
-- applied to the period from the first day of S's deferment to the day before S's death.
-- src:5134 | (1) Subject to paragraph 8, this paragraph applies where—
-- src:5135 | (a) a widow, widower or surviving civil partner (“W”) is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension,
-- src:5136 | (b) W was married to or was the civil partner of the other party to the marriage or civil partnership (“S”) when S died,
-- src:5137 | (c) S’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension was deferred when S died, and
-- src:5138 | (d) S’s entitlement had been deferred throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before S’s death.
@ref sch 5 para 3C(1) (src:5134-5138)
GIVEN `W is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `W was married to or was the civil partner of S when S died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `S’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension was deferred when S died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `S’s pension is a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W’s contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of S’s period of deferment` IS A DATE
      `the day S died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`W is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` AND `W was married to or was the civil partner of S when S died` AND `S’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension was deferred when S died`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this paragraph applies where" (a), (b) and (c)
        IF `sch 5 para 8(4) the conditions in paragraphs 3C(1)(c) and 4(1)(a) are satisfied by S’s pension` `S’s pension is a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W’s contributions` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraph 8", and condition (c) is not satisfied by such a pension
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `sch 5 para 3C(1)(d) S’s entitlement was deferred throughout the 12 months` `the first day of S’s period of deferment` `the day S died`
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 29 February fork of the 12 months (F1)
                  WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                  WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this paragraph applies where ... (d)" is a "where", not an "if"; paragraph 4(1)(c) speaks of this case

-- 3C(1)(d): deferred throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before S's death; the same 12-month count as A1(1).
-- This is the predicate named for the limit (the 12 months): it answers JUST TRUE inside the limit and JUST FALSE short of it, as `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` does,
-- and NOTHING only on the 29 February fork (F1). It is `sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` above that turns a short deferment into NOTHING, because it is introduced by "where".
-- src:5138 | (d) S’s entitlement had been deferred throughout the period of 12 months ending with the day before S’s death.
@ref sch 5 para 3C(1)(d) (src:5138)
GIVEN `the first day of S’s period of deferment` IS A DATE
      `the day S died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 3C(1)(d) S’s entitlement was deferred throughout the 12 months` MEANS
    `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` (Period WITH `the first day` IS `the first day of S’s period of deferment`, `the last day` IS `the day S died` MINUS 1)

-- 3C(2) and (3) as a regulative rule: W shall within the prescribed period elect; lapse is dealt with by 3C(3) (deemed (b) election),
-- so the duty is discharged by the deeming and the lapse leads to FULFILLED, not to a breach.
-- src:5139 | (2) W shall within the prescribed period elect in the prescribed manner either—
-- src:5140 | (a) that paragraph 4 (entitlement to increase of pension) is to apply in relation to S’s period of deferment, or
-- src:5141 | (b) that paragraph 7A (entitlement to lump sum) is to apply in relation to S’s period of deferment.
-- src:5142 | (3) If no election under sub-paragraph (2) is made within the period prescribed under that sub-paragraph, W is to be treated as having made an election under sub-paragraph (2)(b).
@ref sch 5 para 3C(2) and (3) (src:5139-5142)
GIVEN `the prescribed period, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `sch 5 W Party` `sch 5 W Act`
`sch 5 para 3C(2) the election duty` MEANS
    PARTY `sch 5 W the widow, widower or surviving civil partner`
    MUST `sch 5 W makes an election` choice
    WITHIN `the prescribed period, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

-- src:5142 | (3) If no election under sub-paragraph (2) is made within the period prescribed under that sub-paragraph, W is to be treated as having made an election under sub-paragraph (2)(b).
@ref sch 5 para 3C(3) (src:5142)
GIVEN `the election made within the prescribed period` IS A MAYBE `sch 5 Widowed election`
GIVETH A `sch 5 Widowed election`
`sch 5 para 3C(3) the election that is treated as made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the election made within the prescribed period`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `sch 5 para 3C(2)(b) an election that paragraph 7A (the lump sum) applies`
    WHEN JUST chosen THEN chosen

-- 3C(4): regulations (change of election; avoiding duplication of payment): a regulation-making power, inert (machinery).

-- 3C(5): making the (2)(b) election does not affect paragraphs 5 to 6A. A flat negative for the lump-sum election;
-- the (2)(a) election is not spoken to.
-- src:5148 | (5) The making of an election under sub-paragraph (2)(b) does not affect the application of paragraphs 5 to 6A (which relate to an increase in pension where the pensioner’s deceased spouse or civil partner had deferred an entitlement to a guaranteed minimum pension).
@ref sch 5 para 3C(5) (src:5148)
GIVEN election IS A `sch 5 Widowed election`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 3C(5) the election affects the application of paragraphs 5 to 6A` MEANS
    CONSIDER election
    WHEN `sch 5 para 3C(2)(b) an election that paragraph 7A (the lump sum) applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the application of paragraphs 5 to 6A"
    WHEN `sch 5 para 3C(2)(a) an election that paragraph 4 (the increase of pension) applies` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): 3C(5) speaks only of an election under (2)(b)

§§ `Paragraph 4 -- increase where the deceased spouse or civil partner had deferred entitlement`

-- 4(5): the paragraph does not apply where S died before 6 April 1979 and W attained pensionable age before that date.
-- src:5165 | (5) This paragraph does not apply in any case where the deceased spouse died before 6th April 1979 and the widow or widower attained pensionable age before that date.
@ref sch 5 para 4(5) (src:5165)
GIVEN `the day S died` IS A DATE
      W IS A Person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 4(5) this paragraph does not apply` MEANS
    IF (`the day S died` LESS THAN Date 6 4 1979) AND (W's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN Date 6 4 1979)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the case the sub-paragraph names (paragraph 4 does not apply)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph names only a death before 6 April 1979 with W of pensionable age before then

-- 4(1): applies where W is entitled to a Category A or B pension, was married to or the civil partner of S when S died, and one of
-- (a) S was entitled to a Category A or B pension with an increase under this Schedule (but not a Category B pension earned by W's
-- contributions: 8(4)), (b) 3C applies to W and W elected under 3C(2)(a), (c) 3C would apply but for 3C(1)(d) not being met.
-- 4(5) takes away the paragraph in the one case it names. "applies where" is not an "if": otherwise NOTHING.
-- src:5150 | (1) Subject to paragraph 8, this paragraph applies where a widow, widower or surviving civil partner (“W”) is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension and was married to or was the civil partner of the other party to the marriage or civil partnership (“S”) when S died and one of the following conditions is met—
-- src:5151 | (a) S was entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension with an increase under this Schedule,
-- src:5152 | (b) W is a widow, widower or surviving civil partner to whom paragraph 3C applies and has made an election under paragraph 3C(2)(a), or
-- src:5153 | (c) paragraph 3C would apply to W but for the fact that the condition in sub-paragraph (1)(d) of that paragraph is not met.
@ref sch 5 para 4(1) (src:5150-5153)
GIVEN `W is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `W was married to or was the civil partner of S when S died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `S was entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension with an increase under this Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `S’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension was deferred when S died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `S’s pension is a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W’s contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day of S’s period of deferment` IS A DATE
      `the day S died` IS A DATE
      `the election made, or treated as made` IS A MAYBE `sch 5 Widowed election`
      W IS A Person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 4(1) this paragraph applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `sch 5 para 4(5) this paragraph does not apply` `the day S died` W EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph does not apply in any case where the deceased spouse died before 6th April 1979 and the widow or widower attained pensionable age before that date"
        IF NOT (`W is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` AND `W was married to or was the civil partner of S when S died`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies where a widow, widower or surviving civil partner (W) is entitled ... and was married to or was the civil partner of ... (S) when S died"
        IF limbA THEN JUST TRUE
        IF limbB THEN JUST TRUE
        IF limbC THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): none of the conditions (a), (b) or (c) is met
    WHERE
        deferred3C MEANS `sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` `W is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` `W was married to or was the civil partner of S when S died` `S’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension was deferred when S died` `S’s pension is a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W’s contributions` `the first day of S’s period of deferment` `the day S died`
        limbA MEANS `S was entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension with an increase under this Schedule` AND (NOT `S’s pension is a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W’s contributions`)
        limbB MEANS (deferred3C EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the election made, or treated as made` EQUALS JUST `sch 5 para 3C(2)(a) an election that paragraph 4 (the increase of pension) applies`)
        twelveMonths MEANS `sch 5 para A1(1) the period of deferment is at least 12 months` (Period WITH `the first day` IS `the first day of S’s period of deferment`, `the last day` IS `the day S died` MINUS 1)
        limbC MEANS (twelveMonths EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND `S’s entitlement to a Category A or Category B retirement pension was deferred when S died` AND (NOT `S’s pension is a Category B retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled by virtue of W’s contributions`)

-- 4(1A) with 4(3): the amount of the increase of W's pension. Under (1A) it equals the increase to which S was entitled (or, in the
-- cases of (1)(b) and (c), would have been entitled) under this Schedule apart from paragraphs 5 to 6A. Subject to (3): if a married
-- person dies after 5 October 2002, or a civil partner on or after 5 December 2005, the increase is the increase in the basic pension
-- plus one-half of the increase in the additional pension. The two figures are S's (or S's hypothetical) increases, as inputs.
-- src:5154 | (1A) Subject to sub-paragraph (3), the rate of W’s pension shall be increased—
-- src:5155 | (a) in a case falling within sub-paragraph (1)(a), by an amount equal to the increase to which S was entitled under this Schedule, apart from paragraphs 5 to 6A ... ,
-- src:5156 | (b) in a case falling within sub-paragraph (1)(b), by an amount equal to the increase to which S would have been entitled under this Schedule, apart from paragraphs 5 to 6A ... , if the period of deferment had ended immediately before S’s death and S had then made an election under paragraph A1(1)(a), or
-- src:5157 | (c) in a case falling within sub-paragraph (1)(c), by an amount equal to the increase to which S would have been entitled under this Schedule, apart from paragraphs 5 to 6A ... , if the period of deferment had ended immediately before S’s death.
-- src:5158 | (3) If a married person dies after 5th October 2002 or a civil partner dies on or after 5th December 2005, the rate of the retirement pension for that person’s widow, widower or surviving civil partner shall be increased by an amount equivalent to the sum of—
-- src:5159 | (a) the increase in the basic pension to which the deceased spouse or civil partner was entitled; and
-- src:5160 | (b) one-half of the increase in the additional pension.
@ref sch 5 para 4(1A) and (3) (src:5154-5160)
GIVEN `the day S died` IS A DATE
      `S was W’s civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the increase in the basic pension to which S was or would have been entitled under this Schedule, apart from paragraphs 5 to 6A` IS A NUMBER
      `the increase in the additional pension to which S was or would have been entitled under this Schedule, apart from paragraphs 5 to 6A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 4(1A) the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` MEANS
    IF afterTheDate
    THEN basic PLUS (additional DIVIDED BY 2)   -- 4(3): "(a) the increase in the basic pension ...; and (b) one-half of the increase in the additional pension"
    ELSE basic PLUS additional   -- 4(1A): "an amount equal to the increase to which S was entitled under this Schedule"
    WHERE
        basic MEANS `the increase in the basic pension to which S was or would have been entitled under this Schedule, apart from paragraphs 5 to 6A`
        additional MEANS `the increase in the additional pension to which S was or would have been entitled under this Schedule, apart from paragraphs 5 to 6A`
        afterTheDate MEANS
            IF `S was W’s civil partner`
            THEN `the day S died` AT LEAST Date 5 12 2005
            ELSE `the day S died` GREATER THAN Date 5 10 2002

-- 4(4): where orders under section 150 came into force between S's death and W's entitlement, the increase is determined as if
-- they had come into force before the beginning of that period.
-- src:5161 | (4) In any case where—
-- src:5162 | (a) there is a period between the death of the former spouse or civil partner and the date on which the surviving spouse or civil partner becomes entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension, and
-- src:5163 | (b) one or more orders have come into force under section 150 of the Administration Act during that period,
-- src:5164 | the amount of the increase to which the surviving spouse or civil partner is entitled under this paragraph shall be determined as if the order or orders had come into force before the beginning of that period.
@ref sch 5 para 4(4) (src:5161-5164)
GIVEN `there is a period between S’s death and the day W becomes entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more orders have come into force under section 150 of the Administration Act during that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the increase determined on the rates in force when W becomes entitled` IS A NUMBER
      `the increase determined as if the order or orders had come into force before the beginning of that period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 4(4) the amount of the increase to which W is entitled` MEANS
    IF `there is a period between S’s death and the day W becomes entitled` AND `one or more orders have come into force under section 150 of the Administration Act during that period`
    THEN JUST `the increase determined as if the order or orders had come into force before the beginning of that period`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any case where (a) ... and (b) ..."

§§ `Paragraph 5, 5A, 6, 6A and 7 -- increases where the deceased had a guaranteed minimum pension`

-- 7(3): a woman falls within this sub-paragraph if (a) she was married to another woman who at the time of her death was a woman
-- by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate and (b) that marriage subsisted before the certificate was issued.
-- src:5219 | (3) For the purposes of paragraphs 5, 5A and 6A above, a woman falls within this sub-paragraph if—
-- src:5220 | (a) she was married to another woman who, at the time of her death, was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004, and
-- src:5221 | (b) that marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued.
@ref sch 5 para 7(3) (src:5219-5221)
GIVEN `she was married to another woman who, at the time of her death, was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 7(3) the woman falls within this sub-paragraph` MEANS
    IF `she was married to another woman who, at the time of her death, was a woman by virtue of a full gender recognition certificate having been issued under the Gender Recognition Act 2004` AND `that marriage subsisted before the time when that certificate was issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a woman falls within this sub-paragraph if" both (a) and (b)

-- 5(1): applies where W is entitled to a Category A or B pension, was married to or the civil partner of S when S died, and S either
-- was entitled to a guaranteed minimum pension with an increase under section 15(1) of the Pensions Act or would have been if S had
-- retired on the date of S's death. The increase is by the amount that 5(2) sets out.
-- src:5166 | (1) Where—
-- src:5167 | (a) a widow, widower or surviving civil partner (call that person “W”) is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension and was married to or was the civil partner of the other party to the marriage or civil partnership (call that person “S”) when S died, and
-- src:5168 | (b) S either—
-- src:5169 | (i) was entitled to a guaranteed minimum pension with an increase under section 15(1) of the Pensions Act, or
-- src:5170 | (ii) would have been so entitled if S had retired on the date of S’s death,
-- src:5171 | the rate of W’s pension shall be increased by the following amount.
@ref sch 5 para 5(1) (src:5166-5171)
GIVEN `W is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `W was married to or was the civil partner of S when S died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `S was entitled to a guaranteed minimum pension with an increase under section 15(1) of the Pensions Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `S would have been so entitled if S had retired on the date of S’s death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 5(1) this paragraph applies` MEANS
    IF `W is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` AND `W was married to or was the civil partner of S when S died` AND (`S was entitled to a guaranteed minimum pension with an increase under section 15(1) of the Pensions Act` OR `S would have been so entitled if S had retired on the date of S’s death`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where (a) ... and (b) S either (i) ... or (ii) ..."

-- 5(2): which of paragraphs 5A, 6 and 6A sets out the amounts.
DECLARE `sch 5 Paragraph that sets out the amounts` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 para 5(2)(a) the amounts are set out in paragraph 5A`
    `sch 5 para 5(2)(b) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6`
    `sch 5 para 5(2)(c) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6A`

-- src:5172 | (2) The amount is—
-- src:5173 | (a) where W is a woman—
-- src:5174 | (i) whose deceased spouse was a man, or
-- src:5175 | (ii) who falls within paragraph 7(3) below,
-- src:5176 | an amount equal to the sum of the amounts set out in paragraph 5A(2) or (3) below (as the case may be),
-- src:5177 | (b) where W is a man whose deceased spouse was a woman, an amount equal to the sum of the amounts set out in paragraph 6(2), (3) or (4) below (as the case may be) , and
-- src:5178 | (c) where W is—
-- src:5179 | (i) a woman who does not fall within paragraph 7(3) below and whose deceased spouse was a woman;
-- src:5180 | (ii) a man whose deceased spouse was a man; or
-- src:5181 | (iii) a surviving civil partner,
-- src:5182 | an amount equal to the sum of the amounts set out in paragraph (6A)(2) below.
@ref sch 5 para 5(2) (src:5172-5182)
GIVEN W IS A Person
      S IS A Person
      `W is a surviving civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `W falls within paragraph 7(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `sch 5 Paragraph that sets out the amounts`
`sch 5 para 5(2) the paragraph that sets out the amounts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `W is a surviving civil partner` THEN `sch 5 para 5(2)(c) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6A`   -- (c)(iii)
        IF (W's `sex` EQUALS Woman) AND (S's `sex` EQUALS Man) THEN `sch 5 para 5(2)(a) the amounts are set out in paragraph 5A`   -- (a)(i)
        IF (W's `sex` EQUALS Woman) AND `W falls within paragraph 7(3)` THEN `sch 5 para 5(2)(a) the amounts are set out in paragraph 5A`   -- (a)(ii)
        IF (W's `sex` EQUALS Man) AND (S's `sex` EQUALS Woman) THEN `sch 5 para 5(2)(b) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6`   -- (b)
        OTHERWISE `sch 5 para 5(2)(c) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6A`   -- (c)(i) a woman not within 7(3) whose spouse was a woman, or (c)(ii) a man whose spouse was a man

-- The unnumbered paragraph that follows paragraph 7(3) (its number was dropped by the converter) modifies paragraphs 5A to 6A where
-- (a) W became entitled to a Category A or B pension before 6 April 2012 and (b) S died before 6 April 2012. Its (6) says that becoming
-- entitled before 6 April 2012 includes becoming entitled on or after that day to the payment of a pension in respect of a period before it.
-- src:5222 | (1) This paragraph modifies paragraphs 5A to 6A in cases where—
-- src:5223 | (a) W became entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension before 6 April 2012, and
-- src:5224 | (b) S died before 6 April 2012.
-- src:5225 | (“W” and “S” have the same meaning as in paragraph 5.)
-- src:5226 | (2) Paragraph 5A applies as if—
-- src:5227 | (a) in sub-paragraph (2), after paragraph (a), there were inserted—
-- src:5228 | (b) the appropriate amount; and
-- src:5229 | (b) in sub-paragraph (3), after “following—”, there were inserted—
-- src:5230 | (a) one half of the appropriate amount; and
-- src:5231 | (3) Paragraph 6 applies as if—
-- src:5232 | (a) in sub-paragraph (2), after paragraph (a), there were inserted—
-- src:5233 | (b) the appropriate amount; and
-- src:5234 | (b) in sub-paragraph (3), after paragraph (b), there were inserted—
-- src:5235 | (c) the appropriate amount reduced by the amount of any increases under section 109 of the Pensions Act; and
-- src:5236 | (c) in sub-paragraph (4), after paragraph (a), there were inserted—
-- src:5237 | (b) one half of the appropriate amount; and
-- src:5238 | (4) Paragraph 6A applies as if in sub-paragraph (2), after paragraph (a), there were inserted—
-- src:5239 | (b) one half of the appropriate amount; and
-- src:5243 | (6) In sub-paragraph (1)(a) the reference to becoming entitled to a pension before 6 April 2012 includes a reference to becoming entitled on or after that day to the payment of a pension in respect of a period before that day.
@ref sch 5 unnumbered paragraph following paragraph 7(3), sub-paragraphs (1) to (4) and (6) (src:5222-5239) (src:5243)
GIVEN `the day W became entitled to the pension` IS A DATE
      `W became entitled on or after 6 April 2012 to the payment of a pension in respect of a period before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day S died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para after 7(3) the modification of paragraphs 5A to 6A applies` MEANS
    IF ((`the day W became entitled to the pension` LESS THAN Date 6 4 2012) OR `W became entitled on or after 6 April 2012 to the payment of a pension in respect of a period before that day`) AND (`the day S died` LESS THAN Date 6 4 2012)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph modifies paragraphs 5A to 6A in cases where (a) ... and (b) ..."

-- (5) of that paragraph: "the appropriate amount" is the greater of (a) the amount by which the deceased's pension had been
-- increased under section 150(1)(e) of the Administration Act and (b) the amount by which it would have been so increased had the
-- deceased died immediately before W became entitled. It is defined only "in paragraphs 5A to 6A as modified by this paragraph":
-- outside the modified cases the term is undefined in this text (NOTES.md, fork F5).
-- src:5240 | (5) In paragraphs 5A to 6A as modified by this paragraph, the “appropriate amount” means the greater of—
-- src:5241 | (a) the amount by which the deceased person's Category A or Category B retirement pension had been increased under section 150(1)(e) of the Administration Act; or
-- src:5242 | (b) the amount by which his or her Category A or Category B retirement pension would have been so increased had he or she died immediately before the surviving spouse or civil partner became entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension.
@ref sch 5 unnumbered paragraph following paragraph 7(3), sub-paragraph (5) (src:5240-5242)
GIVEN `the modification of paragraphs 5A to 6A applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount by which the deceased person’s pension had been increased under section 150(1)(e) of the Administration Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount by which the pension would have been so increased had the deceased died immediately before W became entitled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para after 7(3) the appropriate amount` MEANS
    IF `the modification of paragraphs 5A to 6A applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (max `the amount by which the deceased person’s pension had been increased under section 150(1)(e) of the Administration Act` `the amount by which the pension would have been so increased had the deceased died immediately before W became entitled`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "the appropriate amount" is defined only in paragraphs 5A to 6A as modified by this paragraph

-- 5A(2) (death before 6 October 2002) and 5A(3) (death after 5 October 2002): the amounts for a woman whose deceased spouse was a man,
-- or who falls within 7(3).
-- src:5183 | (1) This paragraph applies where W (referred to in paragraph 5 above) is a woman—
-- src:5184 | (a) whose deceased spouse was a man, or
-- src:5185 | (b) who falls within paragraph 7(3) below.
-- src:5186 | (2) Where the spouse dies before 6th October 2002, the amounts referred to in paragraph 5(2)(a) above are the following—
-- src:5187 | (a) an amount equal to one-half of the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b) above,
-- src:5188 | (b) the appropriate amount, and
-- src:5189 | (c) an amount equal to any increase to which the spouse had been entitled under paragraph 5 above.
-- src:5190 | (3) Where the spouse dies after 5th October 2002, the amounts referred to in paragraph 5(2)(a) above are the following—
-- src:5191 | (a) one-half of the appropriate amount ... , and
-- src:5192 | (b) one-half of any increase to which the spouse had been entitled under paragraph 5 above.
@ref sch 5 para 5A (src:5183-5192)
GIVEN `the day S died` IS A DATE
      `the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the appropriate amount` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `any increase to which the spouse had been entitled under paragraph 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 5A the sum of the amounts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the appropriate amount`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "the appropriate amount" is used by 5A(2)(b) and 5A(3)(a) and defined only in the modified cases
    WHEN JUST appropriate THEN
        IF `the day S died` LESS THAN Date 6 10 2002
        THEN JUST (((`the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b)` DIVIDED BY 2) PLUS appropriate) PLUS `any increase to which the spouse had been entitled under paragraph 5`)   -- 5A(2)(a), (b), (c)
        ELSE JUST ((appropriate DIVIDED BY 2) PLUS (`any increase to which the spouse had been entitled under paragraph 5` DIVIDED BY 2))   -- 5A(3)(a), (b)

-- 6(2) (wife died before 6 April 1989), 6(3) (after 5 April 1989 but before 6 October 2002), 6(4) (after 5 October 2002): the amounts for a
-- man whose deceased spouse was a woman.
-- src:5193 | (1) This paragraph applies where W (referred to in paragraph 5 above) is a man whose deceased spouse was a woman.
-- src:5194 | (2) Where the wife dies before 6th April 1989, the amounts referred to in paragraph 5(2)(b) above are the following—
-- src:5195 | (a) an amount equal to the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b) above,
-- src:5196 | (b) the appropriate amount, and
-- src:5197 | (c) an amount equal to any increase to which the wife had been entitled under paragraph 5 above.
-- src:5198 | (3) Where the wife dies after 5th April 1989 but before 6th October 2002, the amounts referred to in paragraph 5(2)(b) above are the following—
-- src:5199 | (a) the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b) above, so far as attributable to employment before 6th April 1988,
-- src:5200 | (b) one-half of that increase, so far as attributable to employment after 5th April 1988,
-- src:5201 | (c) the appropriate amount reduced by the amount of any increases under section 109 of the Pensions Act, and
-- src:5202 | (d) any increase to which the wife had been entitled under paragraph 5 above.
-- src:5203 | (4) Where the wife dies after 5th October 2002, the amounts referred to in paragraph 5(2)(b) above are the following—
-- src:5204 | (a) one-half of the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b) above, so far as attributable to employment before 6th April 1988,
-- src:5205 | (b) one-half of the appropriate amount ... , and
-- src:5206 | (c) one-half of any increase to which the wife had been entitled under paragraph 5 above
@ref sch 5 para 6 (src:5193-5206)
GIVEN `the day S died` IS A DATE
      `the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
      `of which, so far as attributable to employment before 6 April 1988` IS A NUMBER
      `of which, so far as attributable to employment after 5 April 1988` IS A NUMBER
      `the appropriate amount` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the increases under section 109 of the Pensions Act` IS A NUMBER
      `any increase to which the wife had been entitled under paragraph 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 6 the sum of the amounts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the appropriate amount`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "the appropriate amount" is used by 6(2)(b), 6(3)(c) and 6(4)(b) and defined only in the modified cases
    WHEN JUST appropriate THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the day S died` LESS THAN Date 6 4 1989
                THEN JUST ((`the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b)` PLUS appropriate) PLUS `any increase to which the wife had been entitled under paragraph 5`)   -- 6(2)(a), (b), (c)
            IF `the day S died` LESS THAN Date 6 10 2002
                THEN JUST ((((`of which, so far as attributable to employment before 6 April 1988` PLUS (`of which, so far as attributable to employment after 5 April 1988` DIVIDED BY 2)) PLUS (appropriate MINUS `the increases under section 109 of the Pensions Act`)) PLUS `any increase to which the wife had been entitled under paragraph 5`))   -- 6(3)(a), (b), (c), (d)
            OTHERWISE JUST (((`of which, so far as attributable to employment before 6 April 1988` DIVIDED BY 2) PLUS (appropriate DIVIDED BY 2)) PLUS (`any increase to which the wife had been entitled under paragraph 5` DIVIDED BY 2))   -- 6(4)(a), (b), (c)

-- 6A(2): the amounts for a woman not within 7(3) whose deceased spouse was a woman, a man whose deceased spouse was a man, or a
-- surviving civil partner.
-- src:5207 | (1) This paragraph applies where W (referred to in paragraph 5 above) is—
-- src:5208 | (a) a woman who does not fall within paragraph 7(3) below and whose deceased spouse was a woman;
-- src:5209 | (b) a man whose deceased spouse was a man; or
-- src:5210 | (c) a surviving civil partner.
-- src:5211 | (2) The amounts referred to in paragraph 5(2)(c) above are the following—
-- src:5212 | (a) one-half of the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b) above, so far as attributable to employment before 6th April 1988,
-- src:5213 | (b) one-half of the appropriate amount ... , and
-- src:5214 | (c) one-half of any increase to which the deceased spouse or civil partner had been entitled under paragraph 5 above.
@ref sch 5 para 6A (src:5207-5214)
GIVEN `of the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b), the part attributable to employment before 6 April 1988` IS A NUMBER
      `the appropriate amount` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `any increase to which the deceased spouse or civil partner had been entitled under paragraph 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 6A the sum of the amounts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the appropriate amount`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "the appropriate amount" is used by 6A(2)(b) and defined only in the modified cases
    WHEN JUST appropriate THEN JUST (((`of the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b), the part attributable to employment before 6 April 1988` DIVIDED BY 2) PLUS (appropriate DIVIDED BY 2)) PLUS (`any increase to which the deceased spouse or civil partner had been entitled under paragraph 5` DIVIDED BY 2))   -- 6A(2)(a), (b), (c)

-- 7(2): an amount calculated under paragraph 5, 5A, 6 or 6A is rounded to the nearest penny, 1/2p going to the next whole penny above;
-- an amount under 1/2p is taken to be zero notwithstanding any other provision.
-- src:5216 | (2) Where an amount is required to be calculated in accordance with the provisions of paragraph 5, 5A, 6 or 6A or sub-paragraph (1) above—
-- src:5217 | (a) the amount so calculated shall be rounded to the nearest penny, taking any 1/2p as nearest to the next whole penny above; and
-- src:5218 | (b) where the amount so calculated would, apart from this sub-paragraph, be a sum less than 1/2p, that amount shall be taken to be zero, notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, the Pensions Act or the Administration Act.
@ref sch 5 para 7(2) (src:5216-5218)
GIVEN `the amount calculated under paragraph 5, 5A, 6 or 6A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 7(2) the amount as rounded` MEANS
    IF `the amount calculated under paragraph 5, 5A, 6 or 6A` LESS THAN 0.005
    THEN 0   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that amount shall be taken to be zero, notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, the Pensions Act or the Administration Act"
    ELSE (FLOOR ((`the amount calculated under paragraph 5, 5A, 6 or 6A` TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 100

-- Paragraph 5 as a whole: the increase of W's pension, for a W to whom 5(1) applies; the amounts of 5A, 6 or 6A as 5(2) directs, rounded by 7(2).
-- src:5166 | (1) Where—
-- src:5167 | (a) a widow, widower or surviving civil partner (call that person “W”) is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension and was married to or was the civil partner of the other party to the marriage or civil partnership (call that person “S”) when S died, and
-- src:5168 | (b) S either—
-- src:5169 | (i) was entitled to a guaranteed minimum pension with an increase under section 15(1) of the Pensions Act, or
-- src:5170 | (ii) would have been so entitled if S had retired on the date of S’s death,
-- src:5171 | the rate of W’s pension shall be increased by the following amount.
-- src:5172 | (2) The amount is—
-- src:5173 | (a) where W is a woman—
-- src:5174 | (i) whose deceased spouse was a man, or
-- src:5175 | (ii) who falls within paragraph 7(3) below,
-- src:5176 | an amount equal to the sum of the amounts set out in paragraph 5A(2) or (3) below (as the case may be),
-- src:5177 | (b) where W is a man whose deceased spouse was a woman, an amount equal to the sum of the amounts set out in paragraph 6(2), (3) or (4) below (as the case may be) , and
-- src:5178 | (c) where W is—
-- src:5179 | (i) a woman who does not fall within paragraph 7(3) below and whose deceased spouse was a woman;
-- src:5180 | (ii) a man whose deceased spouse was a man; or
-- src:5181 | (iii) a surviving civil partner,
-- src:5182 | an amount equal to the sum of the amounts set out in paragraph (6A)(2) below.
@ref sch 5 para 5 (src:5166-5182)
GIVEN W IS A Person
      S IS A Person
      `W is a surviving civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `W falls within paragraph 7(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day S died` IS A DATE
      `W is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `W was married to or was the civil partner of S when S died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `S was entitled to a guaranteed minimum pension with an increase under section 15(1) of the Pensions Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `S would have been so entitled if S had retired on the date of S’s death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b)` IS A NUMBER
      `of which, so far as attributable to employment before 6 April 1988` IS A NUMBER
      `of which, so far as attributable to employment after 5 April 1988` IS A NUMBER
      `the appropriate amount` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the increases under section 109 of the Pensions Act` IS A NUMBER
      `any increase to which the spouse, wife or civil partner had been entitled under paragraph 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 5 the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` MEANS
    IF NOT (`sch 5 para 5(1) this paragraph applies` `W is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension` `W was married to or was the civil partner of S when S died` `S was entitled to a guaranteed minimum pension with an increase under section 15(1) of the Pensions Act` `S would have been so entitled if S had retired on the date of S’s death` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 5(1) does not apply
    ELSE CONSIDER `sch 5 para 5(2) the paragraph that sets out the amounts` W S `W is a surviving civil partner` `W falls within paragraph 7(3)`
         WHEN `sch 5 para 5(2)(a) the amounts are set out in paragraph 5A` THEN rounded (`sch 5 para 5A the sum of the amounts` `the day S died` `the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b)` `the appropriate amount` `any increase to which the spouse, wife or civil partner had been entitled under paragraph 5`)
         WHEN `sch 5 para 5(2)(b) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6` THEN rounded (`sch 5 para 6 the sum of the amounts` `the day S died` `the increase mentioned in paragraph 5(1)(b)` `of which, so far as attributable to employment before 6 April 1988` `of which, so far as attributable to employment after 5 April 1988` `the appropriate amount` `the increases under section 109 of the Pensions Act` `any increase to which the spouse, wife or civil partner had been entitled under paragraph 5`)
         WHEN `sch 5 para 5(2)(c) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6A` THEN rounded (`sch 5 para 6A the sum of the amounts` `of which, so far as attributable to employment before 6 April 1988` `the appropriate amount` `any increase to which the spouse, wife or civil partner had been entitled under paragraph 5`)
    WHERE
        rounded amount MEANS
            CONSIDER amount
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "the appropriate amount" is undefined outside the modified cases
            WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (`sch 5 para 7(2) the amount as rounded` x)

§§ `Paragraphs 7A, 7B, 7C -- the widowed person's or surviving civil partner's lump sum`

-- 7A(1) and (2): applies where W is a person to whom 3C applies and has made (or is treated as having made) a 3C(2)(b) election;
-- W is entitled to the lump sum that 7B calculates.
-- src:5245 | (1) This paragraph applies where a person to whom paragraph 3C applies (“W”) has made (or is treated as having made) an election under paragraph 3C(2)(b).
-- src:5246 | (2) W is entitled to an amount calculated in accordance with paragraph 7B (a “widowed person’s or surviving civil partner's lump sum”).
@ref sch 5 para 7A (src:5245-5246)
GIVEN `paragraph 3C applies to W` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the election made, or treated as made` IS A MAYBE `sch 5 Widowed election`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 5 para 7A(2) W is entitled to a widowed person’s or surviving civil partner’s lump sum` MEANS
    IF (`paragraph 3C applies to W` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the election made, or treated as made` EQUALS JUST `sch 5 para 3C(2)(b) an election that paragraph 7A (the lump sum) applies`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This paragraph applies where a person to whom paragraph 3C applies (W) has made (or is treated as having made) an election under paragraph 3C(2)(b)"

-- 7B(1) and (2): the lump sum is the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period that began at the
-- beginning of S's period of deferment and ended on the day before S's death (the accrual-period rule of paragraph 3B applies to it).
-- 7B(2): "S" is the other party to the marriage or civil partnership, that is the deceased: the inputs about S are about that person.
-- src:5248 | (1) The widowed person’s or surviving civil partner's lump sum is the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period which—
-- src:5249 | (a) began at the beginning of S’s period of deferment, and
-- src:5250 | (b) ended on the day before S’s death.
-- src:5251 | (2) In this paragraph—
-- src:5252 | ‘S’ means the other party to the marriage or civil partnership;
-- src:5254 | ‘accrual period’ means any period of seven days beginning with a prescribed day of the week, where that day falls within S’s period of deferment.
@ref sch 5 para 7B(1) and (2) (src:5248-5252) (src:5254)
GIVEN `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` IS A NUMBER
      `the first day of S’s period of deferment` IS A DATE
      `the day S died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`sch 5 para 7B(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period before S’s death` MEANS
    `sch 5 para 3B(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period of deferment` `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` (Period WITH `the first day` IS `the first day of S’s period of deferment`, `the last day` IS `the day S died` MINUS 1)

-- 7B(1): the lump sum before rounding is the accrued amount; the formula is omitted from this text (see 3B(3)), so the amount is an input.
-- src:5248 | (1) The widowed person’s or surviving civil partner's lump sum is the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period which—
@ref sch 5 para 7B(1) (src:5248)
GIVEN `the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period before S’s death` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 7B(1) the lump sum before rounding` MEANS
    `the accrued amount for the last accrual period beginning during the period before S’s death`

-- 7B(3): the accrued amount for an accrual period for W is given by a formula (in A, P and R) that the converter omitted from this text
-- (the line is followed at once by "where--"), as in 3B(3): the function that would apply it answers NOTHING.
-- 7B(2) defines "accrued amount" as the amount this sub-paragraph calculates, so the definition is cited here.
-- src:5253 | ‘accrued amount’ means the amount calculated in accordance with sub-paragraph (3);
-- src:5255 | (3) The accrued amount for an accrual period for W is—
@ref sch 5 para 7B(2) accrued amount, para 7B(3) (src:5253) (src:5255)
GIVEN `A, the accrued amount for the previous accrual period` IS A NUMBER
      `P, the amount of pension for the accrual period` IS A NUMBER
      `R, the percentage rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 7B(3) the accrued amount for an accrual period` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the formula that combines A, P and R is omitted from this text

-- 7B(3): P is the basic pension, and half of the additional pension, to which S would have been entitled for the accrual period had
-- S's entitlement not been deferred during that period. (A and R are as in 3B(3).)
-- src:5256 | where—
-- src:5257 | A is the accrued amount for the previous accrual period (or, in the case of the first accrual period beginning during the period mentioned in sub-paragraph (1), zero);
-- src:5258 | P is—
-- src:5259 | the basic pension, and
-- src:5260 | half of the additional pension,
-- src:5261 | to which S would have been entitled for the accrual period if his entitlement had not been deferred during the period mentioned in sub-paragraph (1);
@ref sch 5 para 7B(3) P (src:5256-5261)
GIVEN `the basic pension to which S would have been entitled for the accrual period` IS A NUMBER
      `the additional pension to which S would have been entitled for the accrual period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 7B(3) P, the amount of pension for the accrual period` MEANS
    `the basic pension to which S would have been entitled for the accrual period` PLUS (`the additional pension to which S would have been entitled for the accrual period` DIVIDED BY 2)

-- 7B(3) R, (4), (5), (6): R, the timing of a change of base rate, the pension counted, and the section 47(1) reading are in the words
-- of 3B(3), (4), (5) and (6); these functions apply the paragraph 3B rules to S's pension.
-- src:5262 | R is—
-- src:5263 | a percentage rate two per cent. higher than the Bank of England base rate, or
-- src:5264 | if regulations so provide, such higher rate as may be prescribed.
@ref sch 5 para 7B(3) R (src:5262-5264)
GIVEN `the Bank of England base rate, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
      `the higher rate prescribed by regulations, if they so provide` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 7B(3) the percentage rate R` MEANS
    `sch 5 para 3B(3) the percentage rate R` `the Bank of England base rate, in per cent` `the higher rate prescribed by regulations, if they so provide`

-- src:5265 | (4) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (3), any change in the Bank of England base rate is to be treated as taking effect—
-- src:5266 | (a) at the beginning of the accrual period immediately following the accrual period during which the change took effect, or
-- src:5267 | (b) if regulations so provide, at such other time as may be prescribed.
@ref sch 5 para 7B(4) (src:5265-5267)
GIVEN `the day the change in the base rate took effect` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` IS A NUMBER
      `the other time regulations provide, if they so provide` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 5 para 7B(4) the day a change in the base rate is treated as taking effect` MEANS
    `sch 5 para 3B(4) the day a change in the base rate is treated as taking effect` `the day the change in the base rate took effect` `the prescribed day of the week, 0 for Sunday to 6 for Saturday` `the other time regulations provide, if they so provide`

-- src:5268 | (5) For the purposes of the calculation of the widowed person’s or surviving civil partner's lump sum, the amount of Category A or Category B retirement pension to which S would have been entitled for an accrual period—
-- src:5269 | (a) includes any increase under section 47(1) and any increase under paragraph 4 of this Schedule, but
-- src:5270 | (b) does not include—
-- src:5271 | (i) any increase under section 83A or 85 or paragraphs 5 to 6A of this Schedule ... ,
-- src:5272 | (ii) any graduated retirement benefit, or
