@ref sch 5 para 7B(5) (src:5268-5273)
GIVEN pension IS A `sch 5 Weekly pension`
      `the amount prescribed to be left out in prescribed circumstances` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 7B(5) the amount of pension counted for an accrual period` MEANS
    `sch 5 para 3B(5) the amount of pension counted for an accrual period` pension `the amount prescribed to be left out in prescribed circumstances`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not include— (i) any increase under section 83A or 85 or paragraphs 5 to 6A of this Schedule ... , (ii) any graduated retirement benefit, or (iii) in prescribed circumstances, such other amount"

-- src:5274 | (6) The reference in sub-paragraph (5)(a) to any increase under subsection (1) of section 47 shall be taken as a reference to any increase that would take place under that subsection if subsection (2) of that section and section 46(5) of the Pensions Act were disregarded.
@ref sch 5 para 7B(6) (src:5274)
GIVEN `the increase under section 47(1) before the deduction under section 47(2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the increase under section 47(1) actually payable after that deduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 7B(6) the increase under section 47(1) that is counted` MEANS
    `sch 5 para 2(6) the increase under section 47(1) that is counted` `the increase under section 47(1) before the deduction under section 47(2)` `the increase under section 47(1) actually payable after that deduction`

-- 7B(7): where there is a period between S's death and W's entitlement and orders under section 150 came into force in it,
-- the lump sum is increased in accordance with the order or orders (the increase is theirs, so it is an input).
-- src:5275 | (7) In any case where—
-- src:5276 | (a) there is a period between the death of S and the date on which W becomes entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension, and
-- src:5277 | (b) one or more orders have come into force under section 150 of the Administration Act during that period,
-- src:5278 | the amount of the lump sum shall be increased in accordance with that order or those orders.
@ref sch 5 para 7B(7) (src:5275-5278)
GIVEN `there is a period between the death of S and the day W becomes entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one or more orders have come into force under section 150 of the Administration Act during that period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lump sum as increased in accordance with the order or orders` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 7B(7) the lump sum after the orders` MEANS
    IF `there is a period between the death of S and the day W becomes entitled` AND `one or more orders have come into force under section 150 of the Administration Act during that period`
    THEN JUST `the lump sum as increased in accordance with the order or orders`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any case where (a) ... and (b) ..."

-- 7C(1): any lump sum calculated under paragraph 3B or 7B is rounded to the nearest penny, 1/2p going to the next whole penny above.
-- src:5280 | (1) Any lump sum calculated under paragraph 3B or 7B must be rounded to the nearest penny, taking any 1/2p as nearest to the next whole penny above.
@ref sch 5 para 7C(1) (src:5280)
GIVEN `the lump sum calculated under paragraph 3B or 7B` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 5 para 7C(1) the lump sum as rounded` MEANS
    (FLOOR ((`the lump sum calculated under paragraph 3B or 7B` TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 100

-- 7C(2): a duty on the Secretary of State when prescribing a rate (national economic situation; other matters): inert (machinery).

§§ `Paragraph 8 -- married couples and civil partners`

-- 8(5): where S's Category A pension includes an increase under section 51A(2) attributable to W's contributions, the increase or
-- lump sum under 4(1A) or 7A(2) is calculated as if there had been no increase under that section.
-- src:5289 | (5) Where the Category A retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled includes an increase under section 51A(2) attributable to W’s contributions, the increase or lump sum to which W is entitled under paragraph 4(1A) or 7A(2) is to be calculated as if there had been no increase under that section.
@ref sch 5 para 8(5) (src:5289)
GIVEN `the Category A retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled includes an increase under section 51A(2) attributable to W’s contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount calculated with that increase` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount calculated as if there had been no increase under section 51A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`sch 5 para 8(5) the increase or lump sum to which W is entitled under paragraph 4(1A) or 7A(2)` MEANS
    IF `the Category A retirement pension to which S was or would have been entitled includes an increase under section 51A(2) attributable to W’s contributions`
    THEN JUST `the amount calculated as if there had been no increase under section 51A`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the Category A retirement pension ... includes an increase under section 51A(2) attributable to W’s contributions"

-- 8(6): "W" and "S" in sub-paragraphs (4) and (5) have the same meaning as in paragraph 3C, 4 or 7A, as the case requires.
-- The letters' meanings as those paragraphs state them (3C(1)(a) and (b); the letters are repeated in 4(1) and 7B(2)).
DECLARE `sch 5 Letter` IS ONE OF
    `sch 5 para 8(6) the letter W`
    `sch 5 para 8(6) the letter S`

-- src:5290 | (6) In sub-paragraphs (4) and (5), “W” and “S” have the same meaning as in paragraph 3C, 4 or 7A, as the case requires.
@ref sch 5 para 8(6) (src:5290)
GIVEN letter IS A `sch 5 Letter`
GIVETH A STRING
`sch 5 para 8(6) the meaning of the letter` MEANS
    CONSIDER letter
    WHEN `sch 5 para 8(6) the letter W` THEN "a widow, widower or surviving civil partner (W) who is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension"
    WHEN `sch 5 para 8(6) the letter S` THEN "the other party to the marriage or civil partnership (S), who has died"

-- 9 (the paragraph headed "Uprating", numbered by inference): the sums that are the increases in the rates of retirement pensions
-- under this Schedule are subject to alteration by order of the Secretary of State under section 150 of the Administration Act:
-- a power exercised outside these sources; inert (machinery) in NOTES.md.
